{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014BfuUjdbksu2bh8ex2M22o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a self-hosted, single-folder productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a personal productivity system.** It manages tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) as plain **markdown files that are the source of truth** â€” no database, no sync, everything in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`.\n\n- **What it ships â€” a local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders a full interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle + dashboard.** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each with optional notes; the dashboard shows calendar/focus/priorities and per-domain views, all editable in-browser with changes logged.\n\n- **An R&D \"Project Cockpit\" control surface (its biggest feature).** Each project gets a window that runs the **trio** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, server-side terminal sessions. Lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) render as **tiles with one status light** (green/amber/red/grey); clicking a tile **expands an inline panel** with a cached summary on top and a real resizable terminal below.\n\n- **Terminal substrate.** Real interactive **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE fallback), each isolated in its own **git worktree + branch**, with sessions persisted in a durable registry that survives restart. The lane's skill **auto-loads once and greets once** (fixing the old repeating-prompt bug); an engine toggle switches between Claude and Gemini.\n\n- **Supporting R&D machinery.** Cached/validated session + project summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool/service/program/doc), and runnable deliverable previews on a free port hard-guarded â‰  8777.\n\n- **Constraints it holds to.** Python **stdlib-only** with exactly one declared native exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only); all files plain-text/Cowork-accessible; a **daily 5 AM health check** self-tests every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed, never touching live data).\n\n- **Branding.** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool, \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nStatus note from the docs: the R&D surface is at **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 637 tests passing, merged to master 2026-06-13), with v4.1 rebuilding the project-window render clean from the mockup."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48efd110-f051-403a-9e17-d7d79476a90e","uuid":"4a031dec-dd64-4a04-ba13-361c833b227e","request_id":"req_011Cc2LGL3aVcCvyohLF8Yes"}
